// array_add to a resizable array whose count says it has elements but
// whose data is null (issue #158, spec 3.17, 8.4): growing would copy
// those elements from null, so its data is checked as a view's is, and
// the program stops at the built-in's name rather than keeping the count
// over memory nothing wrote.
main :: () {
    a : [..]int;
    a.count = 2;
    array_add(*a, 1);
}
